<item>
            <title>[JGVT-1684] Balance Interface: Retrieve and Add Conditional formatting to Calibration and Verification Due Dates</title>
                <link>https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-1684</link>
                <project id="46901" key="JGVT">TDS - Revvity Signals ELN</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;As a User,&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
I want to be able to check whether my balance is calibrated and verified upon usage,&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
so that&#160; I know whether the balance can be used to conduct a GxP experiment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;Design Notes&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Date/Time format Cal and Ver due dates: dd-MMM-yyyy hh:mm TMZ where TMZ is Local Timezone of logged in User (UCT + x amount of offset time)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Calibration Due Date and Verification Due Date fields are Read-Only Date/Time fields.&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;See Mock-Ups attached
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Metrology metadata Biovia Equipment&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Conditional formatting Cells Interface&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Note: The condition where Calibration and Verification Date&amp;amp;Time = Current Date&amp;amp;Time is kept out of scope, because this edge case is challenging to test and very unlikely to occur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
